# Line endings, stated rather than inferred from whoever cloned the repository.
#
# Without this file the checkout's endings follow the machine's `core.autocrlf`, and on
# Windows that turns every script into a CRLF file: `scripts/run-desktop.sh` then fails with
# `bash\r: No such file`, and the container and CI builds fail on their own scripts the same
# way (the `#!` line carries the \r into the interpreter's name). The sources are the same
# class of problem one step further in — a CRLF `.cppm` is legal C++ but makes every diff
# against an LF clone show whole files changed.
#
# Everything is text and stored LF; only genuinely binary files are exempt.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched: these are compared or passed through byte for byte.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.xz binary

# Scripts must be executable and LF, or they are not scripts.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Windows-only files that Git's own tooling expects with CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
